{"id":"heil","lemma":"heil","pos":"adj","rank":1915,"glosses":["whole; intact; unhurt; safe","sheltered; innocent; ideal"],"ipa":"/haɪ̯l/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/16/De-heil.ogg/De-heil.ogg.mp3","forms":{"comparative":"heiler","superlative":"am heilsten"},"examples":[{"text":"Er ist hier gestern heil angekommen.","en":"He arrived here safely yesterday.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"here"},{"g":"yesterday"},null,{"g":"to arrive","l":"ankommen"}]},{"text":"Ich bin froh, dich heil und ganz zu sehen.","en":"I'm glad to see you in one piece.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"am","l":"sein"},{"g":"glad"},{"g":"you","l":"du"},null,{"g":"and"},{"g":"entire"},{"g":"to / too"},{"g":"to see"}]},{"text":"Wir waren froh zu hören, dass er heil zurück kam.","en":"We were glad to hear that he got back safely.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"to be","l":"sein"},{"g":"glad"},{"g":"to / too"},{"g":"to hear through the ear)"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"he / it"},null,{"g":"stand back!"},{"g":"to come","l":"kommen"}]},{"text":"Es ist ein Wunder, dass unser Haus den Orkan heil überstanden hat.","en":"It's a miracle that our house survived the hurricane.","words":[{"g":"it"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"miracle"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"our"},{"g":"house, building"},{"g":"the","l":"der"},{"g":"hurricane"},null,{"g":"to endure","l":"überstehen"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"}]}]}